            'American and Evergreen Hollies (Ilex): Perhaps the most versatile and landscape-important broadleaf evergreen genus. Glossy, often spiny leaves; red, orange, yellow, or black berries on female plants (male pollinators required for most). Hardy from zones 3 (inkberry) to 9 (Chinese holly). Nellie R. Stevens holly is the most-planted evergreen holly for screening in zones 6–9.',
